# OAuth (not a service account) — a single narrow "drive.file" scope, which
# means this app can only ever touch files IT created. No sharing dance: no
# manual "share this Sheet with a weird email" step, because there's no file
# to share ahead of time — the setup script below creates the folder and
# Sheet itself, under your own Google account.
#
# 1. In Google Cloud Console, create/pick a project and enable the Google
#    Sheets API and Google Drive API.
# 2. APIs & Services -> OAuth consent screen: User type "External", add
#    yourself as a test user, then click "Publish app" (see README — this
#    avoids Google's 7-day refresh-token expiry for apps left in Testing).
#    You'll see an "unverified app" warning when you authorize below — that's
#    expected for a personal app that was never submitted for verification
#    (not needed, since drive.file is a narrow scope and this has one user).
# 3. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create Credentials -> OAuth client ID
#    -> Application type "Desktop app". Copy the Client ID and Client Secret
#    below.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Leave blank, then run `npm run setup:google` FROM YOUR OWN MACHINE (it
# needs to open a real browser — this won't work from a remote/cloud shell).
# It walks you through granting access, then prints the refresh token below
# AND creates the Drive folder + Google Sheet, printing their IDs too — copy
# all three of the vars below from its output.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN=
GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID=
GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID=
